  "evidence": "The finite grammar baseline succeeds on 8/10 worlds. On Normal seed3 and Challenge seed4, each of three fixed controls fails and the combined isolation-plus-minimum protocol completes both native tasks. All arms use 32 new radiation readings per crystal, with navigation/tuning included in action counts.",
  "interpretation": "More repetitions alone did not close these two development failures. This supports further investigation of learned acquisition/preparation programs. It does not establish a new algorithm, general necessity of the combined protocol, or an advantage over ordinary calibration.",
  "design_provenance": "Isolation and minimum aggregation were manually designed after reading the instrument implementation: nonnegative random background and contributions from nearby objects. The learner received only native public readings and reference setpoints; hidden target labels were never supplied.",
  "limitations": [
    "Finite supplied expression grammar, parsers, instrument list, and scripted navigation; not an unrestricted scientific-discovery or LLM-agent result.",
    "Measurement procedures are supplied by the researcher and were not learned. The two follow-up worlds were selected from observed baseline failures.",
    "Instrument randomness is unseeded upstream; arms use fresh episodes, not identical noise draws. No population effect or efficiency estimate from these two worlds.",
    "Do not combine the 8/10 baseline and post hoc 2/2 recovery into a 10/10 result for one predeclared policy.",
    "The short-coefficient prior is well matched to the benchmark generator; it is an ordinary strong baseline, not a universal induction claim."
  ],
  "next_method_candidate": {
    "status": "finite_template_selector_implemented_no_novelty_or_efficiency_advantage",
    "one_sentence": "Learn executable measurement procedures together with the laws they make observable.",
    "concrete_requirement": "Propose preparation/readout programs from public interaction and select them using reference evidence before seeing target outcomes; compare against ordinary calibration and joint model/experiment/observation selection, not only repeated sampling.",
    "novelty_boundary": "Generic experimental design, calibration, or observation-model selection is not new. Requires a distinct synthesis/update operation and transfer beyond this supplied two-by-two menu.",
